    "cohort_manifest": "data/processed/contrastive-cohort-claude-dfd07db-q2-v1.jsonl",
    "cohort_note": "The cohort manifest pinned here defines the study population and the preprocessed images only. The two arms were trained on two manifests whose images and splits are identical; they differ in report text, and the base multilingual manifest additionally retains two studies the translated manifest quarantines. The 56-study gold population resolves identically under both, verified before training.",
    "comparisons": {
      "cohort_contrast": "after_cl/original-multilingual-seed2026/uniform_mean_768 versus after_cl/translated-english-seed2026/uniform_mean_768, paired over the same studies, folds and study resamples, via scripts/analysis/compare_downstream_arms.py",
      "confounded": "uniform pooling also removes the plane_embeddings and plane_attention parameters, so this arm tests pooling and a smaller head together and cannot decompose them. projection_256 is a learned 768->256 linear-plus-GELU compression; a linear probe cannot gain from compression, so this arm is reported but is not evidence against contrastive learning",
      "preregistered_criterion": "All three seed deltas must share a sign and each seed's descriptive 95% interval must exclude zero. Fixed in digest/plane-pooling-protocol.md before the first run and not to be renegotiated.",
      "primary": "after_cl (attention pooling) versus uniform_pooling, per seed, on uniform_mean_768 -- matched pooling at readout and identical dimensionality, so the only difference is how training pooled the planes. Also each against before_cl/uniform_mean_768."
